<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Early Cholas</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 300 CE (approx.) · capital Uraiyur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Sangam-age Chola kings of the Kaveri delta, remembered for the hero Karikala and the great port of Puhar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Cholas</a> were one of the three crowned dynasties of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamilakam">Tamilakam</a>, with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/later-pandyan-empire">Pandyas</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Cheras</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka's</a> edicts in the 3rd century BCE name them among independent peoples to the south of his empire. Their homeland was the fertile Kaveri delta, with an inland capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uraiyur">Uraiyur</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a>, and a port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puhar">Puhar</a>, also called Kaveripattinam.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangam-literature">Sangam</a> poems celebrate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karikala-chola">Karikala</a>, who defeated a coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Cheras</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/later-pandyan-empire">Pandyas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-venni">Venni</a> and is credited by tradition with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kallanai-dam">Kallanai</a>, an early dam across the Kaveri. The poem Pattinappalai describes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puhar">Puhar</a> as a bustling harbour where foreign merchants unloaded horses and goods. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> farming on the delta supported the kingdom, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> adventurers, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellalan">Elara</a>, at times ruled in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From around the 3rd century the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Cholas</a> lost power during the obscure age of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kalabhra-dynasty">Kalabhra dynasty</a> and survived only as local chiefs, later under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pallava-dynasty">Pallava dynasty</a>. The line revived in 848, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayalaya-chola">Vijayalaya</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 300 BCE – 300 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:11.94%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 300 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uraiyur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karikala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tamil folk religion, Vedic religion, Buddhism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Tamil</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sangam Cholas, Early Chola kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=0&amp;focus=early-cholas" aria-label="Early Cholas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6847 1774 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Early Cholas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7167 2030L7198 2018"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7198 2018h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7167 2030h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7167 2030h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Uraiyur. <a href="/atlas?year=0&amp;focus=early-cholas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

